{:edb/db-before-t 1292 :edb/db-after-t 1293 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534605 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:17:33.904Z" 13194139534605 true] [17592186078346 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298346 13194139534605 true] [17592186078346 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298349 13194139534605 true] [17592186078346 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298353 13194139534605 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298325 13194139534605 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298356 13194139534605 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298359 13194139534605 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298363 13194139534605 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298332 13194139534605 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298367 13194139534605 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298370 13194139534605 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298394 13194139534605 true] [17592186078348 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298401 13194139534605 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298339 13194139534605 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298373 13194139534605 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298380 13194139534605 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186298387 13194139534605 true] [17592186078950 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186078950 1100 "Calculate ${\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{3}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186078950 1100 "Calculate $∫_{π/8}^{π/8}\\sin^{3} (\\tan 2x)dx$." 13194139534605 false] [17592186078950 1145 "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\pi /8}^{\\pi /8}{sin}^{3}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x=0\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186078952 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186078952 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{9}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6$, calculate\n${\\int }_{4}^{9}(4f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186078952 1100 "Given that $∫_{9}^{4}f(x)dx = 6$, calculate\n\n$∫_{4}^{9}(4f(x) + 2)dx$." 13194139534605 false] [17592186078952 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{9}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}(4f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{4}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(-6)+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =-24+2(9-4) \\\\  & =-24+10 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298326 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1089 "q-114016" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}(8-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1113 #uuid "30144ba3-8434-5a5c-af65-968cf2badda6" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298325 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(8-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot x\\,{|}_{1}^{3}-6 \\\\  & =8(3-1)-6 \\\\  & =8\\cdot 2-6 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298327 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298328 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298329 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298330 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298331 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1041 "selection" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298327 13194139534605 true] [17592186298326 1110 #uuid "d0f30d74-b006-54e8-b153-75393e79b65e" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298327 1034 "10" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298327 1111 #uuid "d8d13c74-fcd7-50bf-8e98-4bdee8efc3b7" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298328 1034 "6" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298328 1111 #uuid "68a0d81b-531e-5a36-916b-c9c08d33da89" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298329 1034 "-4" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298329 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298329 1111 #uuid "69d810ec-9162-5d1a-a5ae-1e6cabea483e" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298330 1034 "0" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298330 1111 #uuid "47d03ecc-fb00-5ec9-bb1a-043a62257a3d" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298331 1034 "-12" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298331 1111 #uuid "07b15ea4-bf03-5902-8c46-d403337be569" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298333 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1089 "q-114138" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1,$ then what is ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1113 #uuid "61ddbb4e-de49-5742-b133-eb07be0fd7de" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298332 1145 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+1 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(2f(x)-3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-3(3-(-1)) \\\\  & =6-3(4) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298334 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298335 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298336 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298337 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298338 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1041 "selection" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298338 13194139534605 true] [17592186298333 1110 #uuid "9bdfebfc-1c3e-5a02-9e91-b37099a84576" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298334 1034 "1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298334 1111 #uuid "69ea1e3d-dc06-55ac-96cb-198a85cb5968" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298335 1034 "4" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298335 1111 #uuid "40cebf71-b610-58c4-bb42-4fb90ef0f8a6" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298336 1034 "0" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298336 1111 #uuid "9e86906b-6482-5407-b3fb-54277787c5e1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298337 1034 "-2" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298337 1111 #uuid "09d10639-77fe-5cb0-9ab7-f266159f785e" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298338 1034 "-6" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298338 1111 #uuid "f61c1445-0106-59a7-b683-c9035bab95a7" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298340 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1089 "q-114153" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1100 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1113 #uuid "79362d8f-ee8e-5edf-a603-e0c270628ab9" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298339 1145 "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6+(-6) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298341 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298342 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298343 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298344 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298345 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1041 "selection" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298343 13194139534605 true] [17592186298340 1110 #uuid "7eee6eee-0177-5cb2-b1df-c5fa9e98ace8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298341 1034 "8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298341 1111 #uuid "fe5c6322-a33e-5a7f-8039-937d469dbdf3" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298342 1034 "4" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298342 1111 #uuid "12aa52ba-29