uate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{4}{2}^{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298349 1113 #uuid "7ed72a9d-c344-5a6e-a8f7-e12e785b6c21" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298349 1145 "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{4}{2}^{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=0\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298351 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298352 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298352 13194139534605 true] [17592186298350 1110 #uuid "6dd4601b-0aee-56a8-9184-73bfa7cbcb67" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298351 1034 "1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298351 1111 #uuid "60c07373-2118-5f77-8e3c-f0b76f884aec" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298352 1034 "0" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298352 1111 #uuid "9f178c27-18ef-5200-923d-2777a7c53952" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298354 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1089 "q-345634" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1100 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{0}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1113 #uuid "a01d0d55-496a-59f0-876c-6cb1db4e698e" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298353 1145 "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{0}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x=0\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298355 13194139534605 true] [17592186298354 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298354 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298354 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298355 13194139534605 true] [17592186298354 1110 #uuid "1812e228-52dc-5fe2-81f3-feb08a610fa5" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298355 1034 "0" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298355 1111 #uuid "6d39061c-5998-5f0a-97a0-67a9eacaec72" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298357 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1089 "q-346059" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{-3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-3}^{0}(5x-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{0}(5x-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1113 #uuid "a789764d-6c23-5081-bf29-e1cefd94e0a5" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298356 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{-3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}(5x-f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{-3}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{-3}^{0}\\,-\\,(-6) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{0-9}{2}\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{2}\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-\\frac{33}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298358 13194139534605 true] [17592186298357 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298357 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298357 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298358 13194139534605 true] [17592186298357 1110 #uuid "cf2e93b8-c705-5690-ac25-ecf35f01f174" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298358 1034 "-\\frac{33}{2}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298358 1111 #uuid "5a7fbd40-a307-5e2a-9ca7-da314561c49b" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298360 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1089 "q-346061" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{-6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-6}^{6}(3x-9f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{6}(3x-9f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1113 #uuid "06db151f-c6d6-553d-91fa-0c48006d8e64" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298359 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{-6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}(3x-9f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-6}^{6}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,9{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{-6}^{6}\\,-\\,9(-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{6}^{2}-(-6)^{2}}{2}\\,+\\,9 \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0\\,+\\,9 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298361 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298362 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298362 13194139534605 true] [17592186298360 1110 #uuid "4db99a97-3fbd-5b86-9827-4fa550b42518" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298361 1034 "-9" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298361 1111 #uuid "d7bde330-93f8-5288-895c-b37828061946" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298362 1034 "9" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298362 1111 #uuid "cc9ba678-6070-5c6a-bfb8-5719cbb17d1d" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298364 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1089 "q-346181" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{-3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{113}{9},$ calculate ${\\int }_{-3}^{6}(9f(x)+8x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{6}(9f(x)+8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1113 #uuid "443dc647-fc7d-5181-add0-610b67501f3f" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298363 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{-3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{113}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{6}(9f(x)+8x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,8{\\int }_{-3}^{6}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9(-\\frac{113}{9})\\,+\\,8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{-3}^{6} \\\\  & =-113\\,+\\,8\\cdot \\frac{{6}^{2}-(-3)^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-113\\,+\\,8\\cdot \\frac{27}{2} \\\\  & =-113\\,+\\,108 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298365 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298366 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298365 13194139534605 true] [17592186298364 1110 #uuid "32c7b002-864b-5b0e-b82d-79cd606e879a" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298365 1034 "-5" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298365 1111 #uuid "f3a01c27-b258-5f2f-8181-05b3000f48a8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298366 1034 "5" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298366 1111 #uuid "522d036b-4e1a-5bf6-94e7-e1a343f49cc8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298368 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1089 "q-346186" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-10,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1113 #uuid "a02e085b-165a-538f-ae55-e825e6b5f89f" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298367 1145 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n3+(-10)\\,=\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-7.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{11}(2-6f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{2}^{11}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,6{\\int }_{2}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot x{|}_{2}^{11}\\,-\\,6(-7) \\\\  & =2(11-2)+42 \\\\  & =18+42 \\\\  & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298369 13194139534605 true] [17592186298368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298368 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298369 13194139534605 true] [17592186298368 1110 #uuid "06568dec-b3e7-55d9-9f5b-4bc42d6c1c9b" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298369 1034 "60" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298369 1111 #uuid "e1866726-5e6e-5d37-ae66-77a5dd027662" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298371 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1089 "q-346187" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{6}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=11,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1113 #uuid "abacc09f-e24f-5083-9902-ea5b1af36c84" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298370 1145 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-1)+11={\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{10}(6-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{4}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{4}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot x{|}_{4}^{10}-3(10) \\\\  & =6(10-4)-30 \\\\  & =36-30 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298371 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298372 13194139534605 true] [17592186298371 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534605 true] [17592186298371 1041 "field-1" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298371 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298372 13194139534605 true] [17592186298371 1110 #uuid "55dc33ab-63c5-507f-9f01-dd46c490a9e8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298372 1034 "6" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298372 1111 #uuid "01080b51-c0d9-5a7d-9e36-5bc67d4b4cae" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1017 #edb/ref 17592186298374 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1089 "q-4726" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1100 "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=18,{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1113 #uuid "e39e611c-2e6a-5118-851f-9558e33dfe9e" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298373 1145 "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the adjacent intervals rule and substituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the sum rule for definite integrals and substituting the known values, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{7}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 18-10 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x+4 \\\\ 4 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)-g(x))\\text{d}x=4.$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298375 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298376 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298377 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298378 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298379 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1041 "selection" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298379 13194139534605 true] [17592186298374 1110 #uuid "55d599d0-48dd-5bd4-bca8-58ce8dd874e0" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298375 1034 "13" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298375 1111 #uuid "ad292ea9-dd5f-5514-b897-9d26801459df" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298376 1034 "8" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298376 1111 #uuid "5dd4e0dc