 1089 "q-49249" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298394 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534605 true] [17592186298394 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{7}(7+3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298394 1113 #uuid "214f9d44-39be-5f83-8d3d-a2d75b81055a" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298394 1145 "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5)+8={\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3={\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{7}(7+3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{0}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{7}+3(3) \\\\  & =7(7-0)+9 \\\\  & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298396 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298397 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298398 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298399 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1000 #edb/ref 17592186298400 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1041 "selection" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1104 #edb/ref 17592186298399 13194139534605 true] [17592186298395 1110 #uuid "fcf66a86-20a0-5a33-8c18-bb5e8a846bb4" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298396 1034 "67" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298396 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592186298396 1111 #uuid "a4a42881-aada-5097-ae2b-d87549c783dc" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298397 1034 "9" 13194139534605 true] [17592186298397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534605 true] [17592